{"review_context": {"request": {"raw": "vantage-review delta round for PR #1048 (flow 462), on top of r02", "mode": "delta", "flags": ["--vantage-none: all Vantage overlays skipped, keryx repo"]}, "git": {"repo": "MrCipherSmith/keryx", "branch": "feat/conditional-reads", "base": "d6267d4a5099f39b74e86a71e5c8f61ca47aa63d", "head": "5382b56abf17d23db61108554f3c6c68c8e3c036"}, "pr": {"number": 1048, "url": "https://github.com/MrCipherSmith/keryx/pull/1048", "title": "feat: conditional mandatory reads for documents cited by project rules", "state": "open", "base": "main", "head": "feat/conditional-reads", "body": "## Summary\n\nFlow 462: documents cited by project rules (STYLING, THEMING and similar) can now become mandatory reading when the task touches them.\n\n- New declarations file `.metaproject/rules/project/references.json`: per reference a path, glob and keyword conditions, an anchor and a description.\n- `skills resolve-context` takes `--task-text`; a reference whose glob or keyword matches is promoted from on_demand to must_read. Promoted entries are never dropped by the byte cap. A malformed file warns and turns promotion off.\n- Proof of reading: `contracts validate` now checks path, sha256, anchor equal to the declared one, and a summary of at least 40 characters that shares at least three distinct words (five or more letters) with the anchored section. `how: n/a` counts as a miss.\n- `skills references check` and `suggest` (the latter writes no file).\n- TUI: sidebar `refs p/n`, References tab, `/projectctx refs`, states R0\u2013R7.\n- Skill instructions, docs, README and a live-run runbook updated. `docs:check` script added.\n\nOperator decisions: polls 211, 212, 213 (three-word threshold, malformed file stays a warning).\n\nNo version bump and no release (batch releases).\n\n## Known limits\n\n- The summary check is a vocabulary proxy, not proof of understanding.\n- `suggest` output cannot be pasted as is: the loader rejects `bytes`, `anchorCandidates` and empty `globs`/`keywords`.\n- `references-check.ts` has its own citation scan that differs from the resolver's.\n- `src/tui/ci-triage-source.test.ts` has two environment failures that also fail on main.\n- The mkdocs strict build was not run locally (mkdocs not installed).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] CI green\n- [ ] `bun test src/gdskills src/flow src/tui`\n- [ ] Live run on vantage-frontend per `docs/requirements/keryx-conditional-reads/live-run.md` (AC20, operator)\n\n"}, "scope": {"mode": "diff", "files": [".metaproject/core/gdskills/contracts/task-implementer-output-contract.schema.json", ".metaproject/core/gdskills/contracts/tests-creator-output-contract.schema.json", ".metaproject/flows/462-2026-10-18-conditional-reads/acceptance-criteria.md", ".metaproject/flows/462-2026-10-18-conditional-reads/context.md", ".metaproject/flows/462-2026-10-18-conditional-reads/description.md", ".metaproject/flows/462-2026-10-18-conditional-reads/flow.json", ".metaproject/flows/462-2026-10-18-conditional-reads/journal.md", ".metaproject/flows/462-2026-10-18-conditional-reads/plan.md", ".metaproject/flows/462-2026-10-18-conditional-reads/resolved/T10.implement.json", ".metaproject/flows/462-2026-10-18-conditional-reads/resolved/T10.result.json", ".metaproject/flows/462-2026-10-18-conditional-reads/resolved/T11.implement.json", ".metaproject/flows/462-2026-10-18-conditional-reads/resolved/T11.result.json", ".metaproject/flows/462-2026-10-18-conditional-reads/resolved/T12.implement.json", ".metaproject/flows/462-2026-10-18-conditional-reads/resolved/T12.result.json", ".metaproject/flows/462-2026-10-18-conditional-reads/resolved/T13.implement.json", ".metaproject/flows/462-2026-10-18-conditional-reads/resolved/T13.result.json", ".metaproject/flows/462-2026-10-18-conditional-reads/resolved/T5.implement.json", ".metaproject/flows/462-2026-10-18-conditional-reads/resolved/T5.result.json", ".metaproject/flows/462-2026-10-18-conditional-reads/resolved/T6.implement.json", ".metaproject/fl